                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "You're close here but not quite.  You want to put the result of this in a variable so the rest of the function can operate on the array_t, and not the base type.  This removes about 5 + N  type checks from the generated binary, and causes gcc to not generate the exception tables.\n\nnlohmann::json::array_t* arr = value.get_ptr<nlohmann::json::array_t*>();\nif (arr == nullptr){\n   return false;\n}\n\nif (arr->empty()){\n   return true;\n}\n\nnlohmann::json::value_t firstType = arr->begin()->type() =="
